    "plain_text": "Sir Richard Ashmole Cooper was a British industrialist who led his family’s animal-health chemicals business from 1913 until his death. He combined that commercial role with politics, representing Walsall in Parliament for twelve years and helping to found the National Party. Under his chairmanship, the company became Cooper, McDougall & Robertson.",
